# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# WHAT READS THIS FILE: `npm run build` and `npm run gates`, both of which run
# node with --env-file-if-exists=.env. Nothing else does, `npm test` included,
# so a local .env can never change a test result. If you would rather not keep
# a file, put the variables on the command line instead and remember that the
# gates need PROFILE_FORBIDDEN_NAMES as well as the build does.
#
# A GitHub user token. Measured 2026-10-02: the repo scope is enough for your own
# figures, and read:user is NOT required for them. A token scoped
# gist, read:org, repo, workflow, with no read:user, returned the whole
# contribution calendar. read:user is only needed to read a DIFFERENT user's
# contributions, or to include restricted ones. See docs/spec.md 5.2.
#
# The workflow's built-in GITHUB_TOKEN is still assumed not to do, and that half
# is unverified: it is an installation token scoped to one repository rather than
# a user token, the contribution calendar lives behind contributionsCollection,
# and private contributions are only counted for the token's own owner.
#
# The same value goes into the repo's Actions secrets under this name, for the
# daily refresh workflow.
PROFILE_GH_TOKEN=

# OPTIONAL. Comma separated strings that must never reach a published file.
#
# ADR 0001's tree scan is opt-in as of its 2026-10-02 amendment: the owner
# weighed their own name and chose not to configure one. Left unset, the scan
# passes carrying a note that it scanned for nothing, which is deliberately not
# the same statement as "the tree is clean", and neither a local build nor the
# daily refresh is held back by it. Set it and the scan runs over every file a
# commit could carry and FAILS on a hit; the same value goes into the repo's
# Actions secrets under this name.
#
# The name goes on the RIGHT of the =. A name written as a key sets nothing, and
# `npm run gates` now says so distinctly rather than reporting the scan as
# unconfigured, because those two look identical from the outside.
#
# Do not put the handle or the login here. Those are what the profile exists to
# show, so they are in the copy, the README and both assets by design, and the
# gate fails naming that contradiction.
PROFILE_FORBIDDEN_NAMES=
